layout: changelog
title: Security updates for self-hosted Appwrite
date: 2026-10-21
cover: /images/changelog/2026-10-08-1.avif
tags: security, infrastructure
---

Appwrite 2.6.0 and 1.9.8 include security updates for self-hosted deployments.

Both releases update outbound HTTPS certificate trust to reject the compromised eMudhra certificate chains described in [Cloudflare's disclosure](https://blog.cloudflare.com/emudhra-certificate-compromise/). TLS verification remains enabled.

- **2.x installations:** upgrade to [Appwrite 2.6.0](https://github.com/appwrite/appwrite/releases/tag/2.6.0) using the [latest upgrade instructions](/docs/advanced/self-hosting/production/updates#upgrading-to-latest).
- **1.9 installations:** upgrade to [Appwrite 1.9.8](https://github.com/appwrite/appwrite/releases/tag/1.9.8) using the [1.9 upgrade instructions](/docs/advanced/self-hosting/production/updates#upgrading-1-9). This patch also updates the SVG sanitizer to 1.1.1 and refreshes cached avatar and preview responses.

Back up your instance before upgrading and run the migration afterward. Appwrite 2.6.0 includes schema updates; 1.9.8 introduces no schema changes. Endpoints still presenting a compromised certificate chain must replace their certificates before Appwrite can connect to them.

The linked GitHub release notes include the complete changes bundled with each version.
